---
// The account-deletion URL for the Play Console Data safety form. Google needs
// a page reachable without installing the app that names the app, gives the
// steps, and says what is deleted and what is kept.
//
// What is deleted / kept must match supabase/functions/delete-account and
// migration 20260914000001. Change them together.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, mailto } from '../site';
---

<Base
  title="Delete your account"
  description="How to delete your PadiLearn account and data, and what happens when you do."
>
  <article class="container prose page">
    <h1>Delete your PadiLearn account</h1>
    <p>
      You can delete your <strong>PadiLearn</strong> account and the data linked to it at any
      time, from inside the app or by email.
    </p>

    <h2>Option 1: in the app</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open the PadiLearn app and sign in.</li>
      <li>Go to your <strong>Profile</strong>.</li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Delete account</strong>.</li>
      <li>Type <strong>DELETE</strong> to confirm, then tap <strong>Delete account</strong>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Your account is deleted straight away and you are signed out.</p>

    <h2>Option 2: by email</h2>
    <p>
      If you can't use the app, email <a href={mailto('Delete my PadiLearn account')}>{site.supportEmail}</a>
      from the email address on your account, with the subject
      <strong>"Delete my PadiLearn account"</strong>. We'll confirm the request is yours and delete the
      account within 30 days.
    </p>

    <h2>What gets deleted</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your account, name, email address and password</li>
      <li>Your profile photo</li>
      <li>Your enrolments and lesson progress</li>
      <li>Your comments, ratings and notifications</li>
      <li>Payout bank details (teachers)</li>
      <li>Courses you created, with their videos and thumbnails (teachers)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we keep</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Purchase records</strong>, with your account link removed, for our financial and tax
        records.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Reports you made</strong> about content, so we can finish reviewing them.
      </li>
      <li>
        Copies in our hosting provider's <strong>backups</strong> for a short period, until they are
        overwritten.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="callout">
      <p>
        <strong>Teachers whose students paid for a course:</strong> the app can't delete these
        accounts automatically, because deleting your courses would remove what those students paid
        for. Email <a href={mailto('Delete my PadiLearn teacher account')}>{site.supportEmail}</a> and
        we'll sort out your students' access first, then delete your account.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Delete some data, not the whole account</h2>
    <p>
      In the app you can delete your own comments and notifications, and teachers can delete their
      courses and payout details. For anything else, such as your profile photo, email <a href={mailto('Delete some of my PadiLearn data')}>{site.supportEmail}</a> and
      tell us what you'd like removed.
    </p>

    <p>
      More detail is in our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-block: 3rem 1rem;
  }
</style>
